This site is Astro plus Sanity. `city` and `tip` are the only document types.

- Schemas live in `src/sanity/schemaTypes/`.
- GROQ queries live in `src/lib/queries.ts` and use `defineQuery` so `npm run typegen` can type them.
- Do not put a Sanity token in a `PUBLIC_` or `SANITY_STUDIO_` variable.
- Published content in project `p4yybrla`, dataset `production`, is crew-written: Accra, Brussels, Doha, Dubai, and Johannesburg (25 tips). The live site is https://n-blessing.github.io/crew-layover-guide/ and Studio is https://crew-layover-guide.sanity.studio/. `seed/seed.ndjson` (Brussels, Dubai, Lagos, Nairobi, `EXAMPLE:` titles) is only the offline fallback. Do not describe that seed as the published site.
- New unverified sample tips stay `isExample: true`, with titles that start `EXAMPLE:`, until a person replaces them with notes they have checked. Crew-written published tips are not sample copy.

Official Sanity wiring for Cursor, taken from current Sanity docs:

- This repo's `.cursor/mcp.json` points at `https://mcp.sanity.io`. Cursor will ask for OAuth. The same server can be installed with `npx sanity@latest mcp configure`.
- Agent skills install with `npx skills add sanity-io/agent-toolkit` (Node.js 22.20 or later). In Cursor chat, `/add-plugin sanity` installs the marketplace plugin.
- Sanity's documentation index for agents is https://www.sanity.io/docs/llms.txt

After a schema or query change, run `npm run typegen` and commit `schema.json` and `src/sanity/sanity.types.ts`.
